From 02ac5429ce8c42c56e7b09458a928f29f48c4903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jared Massie <you@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 07:09:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Re-apply dropped tappable-link + reliable-mailer fix, add
 on-device debug log
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The earlier phone-applied patch reported success but silently dropped most
of its content on GitHub (AndroidManifest queries block, the fixed
TamperAlertMailer SMTP client, pubspec's url_launcher dep, and the Settings
tappable-link UI never actually landed) — restoring all of that here.

Also adds DebugLog: a small on-device ring-buffer log written from the
accessibility/VPN services (onServiceConnected, every blocking decision,
onDestroy/onRevoke, DNS allow/block decisions) and readable from a new
"Debug Log" section in Settings, so enforcement bugs can be diagnosed
without adb/root — which the previous debugging attempt got stuck on.
